WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0059: a figure waiting for its maps is lit in WoW's units (beta item 10, part of 9).

- Patch 0052 took WoW's light to linear for BG3's own lighting of a figure (flag 32), because WoW's
  models multiply a gamma-space texel by `lit` while her albedo is sampled linear. The other half was
  left as it was: patch 0006's law (`tav_a.x < 0` in `wow_model.wgsl`), which every mesh is drawn by
  until tavtex has baked its G-buffer maps, and which `WOW_BG3_TAV_SHADE=wow` uses for all of them.
  There her linear albedo stands in for the gamma byte WoW's law multiplies, so a mesh shows
  `albedo_linear x lit` where it should show `srgb(albedo) x lit`: 2 to 4 times too dark, and most of
  that in the dark channels, so the figure is too dark and too saturated as well.
- That is what the 0.1.0 playtest showed (item 10, "clothes and parts of the model (Gale's
  face very dark) take a long time to get WoW's lighting", and item 9's "new companions especially"):
  his own logs show the state lasting tens of seconds. tavtex.log of his cold 12:52 session: the
  first plan had 6 of 40 meshes baked, 13 of 40 after 26 s, 40 of 40 after 56 s, with 23 G-buffer
  maps still to go, and benilla's own log says "34 meshes had no maps after 12 s: drawn untextured".
  A mesh's look therefore walks four states: hidden, untextured, albedo under the law (too dark),
  and BG3's lighting. This patch makes the third state agree with the fourth in brightness.
- `wow_model.wgsl`: flag 64 (set with flag 16) takes her albedo to gamma for the law path, so it
  writes `srgb(albedo) x lit`, the units of WoW's own models and of flag 32's result. A `tavdebug`
  view keeps the old value, so captures beside BG3's frame stay comparable with the earlier runs.
- `wowbg3_tav.rs`: `WOW_BG3_TAV_LAW=linear` turns flag 64 off (the look before this patch), with a
  log line for the choice, and the maps line now counts the meshes still drawn by the law
  ("N by patch 0006's law: no G-buffer maps baked yet"), which measures how long the state lasts.
- Not touched: BG3's own lighting (flag 32), the bake times themselves (tavtex), and the 12 s
  untextured fallback.

